## What this session added (the browser half of Milestone 3)

**Crypto library** — [apps/web/src/lib/crypto](apps/web/src/lib/crypto), client-side only on `libsodium-wrappers-sumo`: [vault.ts](apps/web/src/lib/crypto/vault.ts) (Argon2id KEK → wrapped vault key → recovery verifier), [file-format.ts](apps/web/src/lib/crypto/file-format.ts) (single-pass encryptor with incremental hashing; a streaming decryptor that reassembles exact chunk boundaries and rejects reordered/truncated/extended streams), plus committed [test-vectors.ts](apps/web/src/lib/crypto/test-vectors.ts).

**Upload path** — [pipeline.ts](apps/web/src/features/uploads/pipeline.ts) (framework-free: create → encrypt/stream chunks → finalize with the declared hashes, resume via `receivedChunkNumbers`, cancel), a fetch [transport](apps/web/src/features/uploads/transport.ts), and eight Next route handlers under [src/app/api](apps/web/src/app/api) that attach the httpOnly token server-side — the browser still never sees it (ADR-017).

**UI** — vault create/unlock/lock card in Settings with a real status badge, a Telegram connect flow (phone → code → 2FA, check, disconnect), an Upload button + drop target gated on the vault, a floating queue panel with per-file progress/cancel/retry, and Download & decrypt in the details dialog. Stale "arrives in a later milestone" copy across dashboard, library and storage status now matches what ships.

**Docs** — [format doc §4–6](docs/architecture/encryption-format.md) (hashes declared at finalize; vectors describe what is actually committed), [ADR-017](docs/architecture/decisions.md) path list corrected, [local-development.md](docs/setup/local-development.md) storage + upload walkthrough, [README](README.md) status/scripts/security model, [.env.example](apps/api/.env.example) storage vars, and the new [milestone-3.md](docs/reports/milestone-3.md) report.

## Checks actually run

- `pnpm typecheck` — contracts, API, web all pass.
- `pnpm test` — **API 122/122** (12 files), **web 69/69** (8 files), including the new upload-pipeline, crypto-vector and file-format suites.
- `pnpm build` — production build passes; all eight new `/api/*` routes register.
- `pnpm db:migrate` — 12 migrations applied, `0010` consistency checks hold.
- **Browser end-to-end**: sign in → create vault (`POST /api/encryption/vault` 200) → drop a 2,600,000-byte file → 3 chunks confirmed → *Encrypted and stored* → server shows `contentStatus: ready`, version with `ciphertextSize = 2,600,075`, storage object exactly 2,600,075 bytes, **zero staging leftovers** → Download & decrypt returned a blob **byte-for-byte identical** to the original. Locked-vault gating and the wrong-passphrase copy were exercised too.

One honesty note: a `dashboard-cards.test.tsx` assertion failed once during a full parallel run that coincided with the working tree being committed (line-ending normalisation touched a source file mid-run). It passes in isolation and in two consecutive full runs afterwards; I changed nothing to make it pass.

## Limitations

Telegram was verified only against an injected fake client — a real account test needs `STORAGE_PROVIDER=telegram` plus the three env vars. Pause/prioritise/source-reselection UI, previews and version history are Milestone 4+. The vault key lives in page memory only, so a reload locks it (documented).

Both dev servers (`pnpm dev:api` on 8787, `pnpm dev:web` on 3000) are still running since you were testing through them. Two files remain uncommitted: [milestone-3.md](docs/reports/milestone-3.md) and a stale-comment fix in [seed-cli.ts](apps/api/src/database/seed-cli.ts) — I've left committing to you.
